I personally only do the protection racket with Gnomish Healers, and
even then, I usually only get a couple points of protection, because I
generally only donate my starting gold.  If I get to Minetown with a
gold amount of something like 1500, then maybe I'll sell a couple
things to get up to 1600 gold; but I'm not going to spend a bunch of
turns trying to get all the money from the shopkeepers.

Having said all that, I don't think it overall increases my ascension
rate.  However, I do think it's an interesting way to play Gnomish
Healers -- so I will do the protection racket for the sake of fun.
Also, since I'm doing a really watered-down version of the protection
racket, it doesn't take much real-time for me to do -- and since I'm
doing this at the beginning of the game, even if I do die it doesn't
matter very much.

I think my playstyle is more geared toward winning games in a decent
amount of time, as opposed to getting the highest winrate possible.  I
might not have a super awesome winrate, but I can pump out ascensions
at a decent real-time, even if you include the real-time I spend on
games that I lose.


